{
  "$comment": [
    "How every picture on README.md and README.pl.md was made. `deno task docs` replays this file:",
    "one CLI run per entry writing <out>.svg, then `rsvg-convert -w <width>` writing <out>.png.",
    "`width` is the PNG width in pixels; the height follows the SVG's aspect ratio.",
    "`keepSvg: false` means the drawing is too large to belong in the repository (README says so",
    "in the text next to it), so only the PNG is written and the SVG goes to a temporary file.",
    "`handMade` lists the pictures this file deliberately does NOT cover: they were drawn by hand",
    "and no CLI invocation reproduces them."
  ],
  "images": [
    { "out": "hero", "flags": ["--width=40", "--height=40", "--seed=7"], "width": 700 },
    {
      "out": "tiny-colorized",
      "flags": ["--width=8", "--height=8", "--seed=7", "--colored"],
      "width": 420
    },
    { "out": "tiny", "flags": ["--width=8", "--height=8", "--seed=7"], "width": 420 },
    { "out": "portrait", "flags": ["--width=20", "--height=40", "--seed=7"], "width": 420 },
